# The sparse sequence twin, rerun after the dispatch fix.
#
# sae_tokens is both sparse and a sequence, so branch order decides its loader.
# The ProcessBench block tested `seq` before `sparse_seq`, handed these cells a
# dense SpanLoader, and all four died at scoring AFTER completing their
# hyperparameter search. Fixed, with a test pinning the order at both dispatch
# sites.
#
# This is the one sparse cell that never pools away per-token structure, so it is
# where SAE features would be expected to do best: the pooled twins lose between
# 0.053 and 0.195, and the loss shrinks the more tokens are pooled.

sae_tokens attn_query
sae_tokens transformer:d256,l2,f1024,h4
